1
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Dog Sitting Request

2
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:16,426
Mr. Takahashi, do you have a moment?

3
00:00:16,449 --> 00:00:19,116
Yes, what's up?

4
00:00:19,139 --> 00:00:22,492
What can I do for you?

5
00:00:22,515 --> 00:00:29,648
I’ve suddenly been assigned to a business trip abroad.

6
00:00:29,671 --> 00:00:33,439
That sounds tough.

7
00:00:33,462 --> 00:00:36,496
Yes, what's up?

8
00:00:36,519 --> 00:00:40,853
Starting next Monday.

9
00:00:40,876 --> 00:00:45,145
How long will you be gone?

10
00:00:45,168 --> 00:00:48,868
For a week.

11
00:00:48,891 --> 00:00:53,028
That’s quite a while.

12
00:00:53,052 --> 00:00:55,986
Yeah.

13
00:00:56,009 --> 00:01:00,395
So, I have a favor to ask.

14
00:01:00,418 --> 00:01:03,952
What can I do for you?

15
00:01:03,975 --> 00:01:11,759
Would you mind taking care of my dog while I’m away?

16
00:01:11,782 --> 00:01:14,416
Your dog?

17
00:01:14,439 --> 00:01:17,357
Yes, what's up?

18
00:01:17,380 --> 00:01:20,962
It’s a small breed.

19
00:01:20,986 --> 00:01:26,286
I’ve never owned a dog before.

20
00:01:26,309 --> 00:01:29,906
Don’t worry.

21
00:01:29,929 --> 00:01:33,996
He’s a very calm dog.

22
00:01:34,019 --> 00:01:38,319
What about feeding?

23
00:01:38,342 --> 00:01:43,442
I’ll prepare all the food.

24
00:01:43,465 --> 00:01:47,131
Does he need walks?

25
00:01:47,154 --> 00:01:50,055
Yes, what's up?

26
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:54,213
Yes, please take him out in the morning and evening.

27
00:01:54,236 --> 00:02:00,702
I might worry about him during meetings.

28
00:02:00,725 --> 00:02:05,722
He’ll sleep quietly in his cage.

29
00:02:05,746 --> 00:02:09,012
I see.

30
00:02:09,035 --> 00:02:13,069
Of course, I’ll pay you for your trouble.

31
00:02:13,092 --> 00:02:16,158
Understood.

32
00:02:16,181 --> 00:02:19,215
I’ll take care of him.

33
00:02:19,238 --> 00:02:22,075
Thank you so much.

34
00:02:22,098 --> 00:02:25,199
That’ll really help.

35
00:02:25,222 --> 00:02:29,289
What’s your dog’s name?

36
00:02:29,312 --> 00:02:33,050
His name is Pochi.

37
00:02:33,073 --> 00:02:38,506
Can I see Pochi once over the weekend?

38
00:02:38,529 --> 00:02:41,863
Understood.

39
00:02:41,886 --> 00:02:44,619
I’ll bring him by.

40
00:02:44,642 --> 00:02:48,954
Is there anything I need to prepare?

41
00:02:48,978 --> 00:02:52,878
Nope, nothing.

42
00:02:52,901 --> 00:02:56,854
I’ll bring everything.

43
00:02:56,878 --> 00:03:00,269
Understood.

44
00:03:00,292 --> 00:03:01,792
Scene 2: Meetup Gone Wrong

45
00:03:01,792 --> 00:03:06,567
Hello? Where are you right now?

46
00:03:06,591 --> 00:03:11,891
I’m standing in front of the sign next to the café.

47
00:03:11,914 --> 00:03:16,014
I should be there too.

48
00:03:16,037 --> 00:03:21,221
That’s weird. I don’t see you at all.

49
00:03:21,244 --> 00:03:25,078
You should see a big clock.

50
00:03:25,101 --> 00:03:29,167
I don’t see a clock.

51
00:03:29,190 --> 00:03:34,424
Then we must be in the wrong place.

52
00:03:34,447 --> 00:03:39,234
I came out of the East Exit of the subway, right?

53
00:03:39,258 --> 00:03:44,737
No, it’s the West Exit.

54
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,594
Huh?

55
00:03:47,617 --> 00:03:50,523
It was the West Exit.

56
00:03:50,546 --> 00:03:56,697
I sent you a message saying ‘West Exit.’

57
00:03:56,721 --> 00:04:01,308
Sorry, I wasn’t paying attention.

58
00:04:01,331 --> 00:04:05,966
Should I head to the west exit now?

59
00:04:05,989 --> 00:04:10,656
No, I’ll come over there.

60
00:04:10,679 --> 00:04:13,745
I know the way.

61
00:04:13,768 --> 00:04:18,084
I think it’ll be fine.

62
00:04:18,107 --> 00:04:22,541
Turn right at the convenience store.

63
00:04:22,564 --> 00:04:25,752
Got it, the convenience store.

64
00:04:25,775 --> 00:04:28,285
Understood.

65
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:31,679
I’ll wait there.

66
00:04:31,702 --> 00:04:34,248
Thanks.

67
00:04:34,272 --> 00:04:37,226
I’ll hurry over.

68
00:04:37,249 --> 00:04:40,683
You don’t need to run.

69
00:04:40,706 --> 00:04:44,372
I’m really sorry.

70
00:04:44,395 --> 00:04:47,731
Be careful on your way.

71
00:04:47,754 --> 00:04:51,705
How long do you think it’ll take?

72
00:04:51,728 --> 00:04:56,262
It should take about 5 minutes on foot.

73
00:04:56,285 --> 00:04:58,619
Understood.

74
00:04:58,642 --> 00:05:02,190
I’ll call you again when I arrive.

75
00:05:02,213 --> 00:05:06,596
I’ll wait right here without moving.

76
00:05:06,620 --> 00:05:08,688
Yeah.

77
00:05:08,712 --> 00:05:11,217
Please.

78
00:05:11,241 --> 00:05:14,607
See you later.

79
00:05:14,630 --> 00:05:17,805
I’ll be there soon.

80
00:05:17,829 --> 00:05:19,329
Scene 3: Changing a Hotel Reservation by Phone

81
00:05:19,329 --> 00:05:24,763
Hello, this is Sakura Hotel.

82
00:05:24,786 --> 00:05:30,419
I’d like to change my hotel reservation.

83
00:05:30,442 --> 00:05:33,342
Understood.

84
00:05:33,365 --> 00:05:38,148
May I have your name, please?

85
00:05:38,172 --> 00:05:41,705
It’s Tanaka.

86
00:05:41,728 --> 00:05:44,962
Mr. Tanaka, correct?

87
00:05:44,984 --> 00:05:48,284
Please hold on.

88
00:05:48,307 --> 00:05:51,141
Yes, what's up?

89
00:05:51,164 --> 00:05:57,830
You have a reservation from Friday next week for 2 nights.

90
00:05:57,853 --> 00:06:00,487
Yes, what's up?

91
00:06:00,510 --> 00:06:06,379
Can I change it to a 1-night stay on Sunday?

92
00:06:06,402 --> 00:06:11,769
A Sunday stay, correct?

93
00:06:11,792 --> 00:06:14,958
Is it available?

94
00:06:14,981 --> 00:06:17,536
Yes, what's up?

95
00:06:17,559 --> 00:06:21,793
We can prepare a room for you.

96
00:06:21,816 --> 00:06:25,974
How will the fee change?

97
00:06:25,997 --> 00:06:31,964
Sunday has a discount rate.

98
00:06:31,987 --> 00:06:35,960
How much will it be?

99
00:06:35,984 --> 00:06:40,817
It’s 8,000 yen per night.

100
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:44,151
Understood.

101
00:06:44,175 --> 00:06:48,718
Would you like to add breakfast?

102
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:52,607
How much is breakfast?

103
00:06:52,630 --> 00:06:57,001
It’s 1,000 yen.

104
00:06:57,025 --> 00:07:00,407
What’s on the menu?

105
00:07:00,430 --> 00:07:06,137
You can choose between Japanese or Western-style breakfast.

106
00:07:06,161 --> 00:07:10,428
Then, I’ll take breakfast as well.

107
00:07:10,451 --> 00:07:14,084
Understood.

108
00:07:14,107 --> 00:07:18,086
What time is check-in?

109
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:22,876
Check-in is from 3 PM.

110
00:07:22,899 --> 00:07:27,698
Can I drop off my luggage in advance?

111
00:07:27,722 --> 00:07:30,588
Yes, what's up?

112
00:07:30,611 --> 00:07:34,486
We’ll hold it at the front desk.

113
00:07:34,509 --> 00:07:37,694
Understood.

114
00:07:37,717 --> 00:07:43,685
We’ll send you a detailed confirmation via email.

115
00:07:43,709 --> 00:07:46,776
Please.

116
00:07:46,799 --> 00:07:51,947
I'll send it as soon as it's ready.

117
00:07:51,970 --> 00:07:55,081
I appreciate your help.

118
00:07:55,105 --> 00:07:58,771
Looking forward to it.

119
00:07:58,794 --> 00:08:00,294
Scene 4: The Spark That Started My Volunteering Journey

120
00:08:00,294 --> 00:08:07,473
Mr. Yamada, how long have you been volunteering?

121
00:08:07,497 --> 00:08:11,763
About half a year now.

122
00:08:11,786 --> 00:08:16,253
What kind of activities do you do?

123
00:08:16,276 --> 00:08:20,976
I pick up trash in the neighborhood.

124
00:08:20,999 --> 00:08:25,032
Why did you start?

125
00:08:25,055 --> 00:08:29,822
Moving here was the trigger.

126
00:08:29,845 --> 00:08:33,278
You moved here?

127
00:08:33,301 --> 00:08:40,134
Yes. I wanted to get to know this town better.

128
00:08:40,157 --> 00:08:44,524
So that's why you joined, huh?

129
00:08:44,547 --> 00:08:50,647
Yeah. Now I even chat with my neighbors.

130
00:08:50,670 --> 00:08:55,417
That's wonderful.

131
00:08:55,441 --> 00:09:00,547
At first, it was tough getting up early.

132
00:09:00,571 --> 00:09:05,329
Do you gather early in the morning?

133
00:09:05,352 --> 00:09:10,731
Every Sunday at 7 AM.

134
00:09:10,755 --> 00:09:14,723
That's early.

135
00:09:14,746 --> 00:09:20,715
But now I'm used to waking up early.

136
00:09:20,738 --> 00:09:24,772
It's good for my health too.

137
00:09:24,795 --> 00:09:30,110
Yeah, and it keeps the town clean.

138
00:09:30,133 --> 00:09:35,969
How do you feel about people who litter?

139
00:09:35,993 --> 00:09:40,174
It makes me sad.

140
00:09:40,197 --> 00:09:43,864
I see.

141
00:09:43,887 --> 00:09:51,323
But instead of getting angry, I want to keep cleaning up.

142
00:09:51,347 --> 00:09:55,424
Can I join too?

143
00:09:55,447 --> 00:09:58,881
Of course!

144
00:09:58,904 --> 00:10:02,455
Anyone can participate.

145
00:10:02,478 --> 00:10:06,711
Do I need to sign up?

146
00:10:06,734 --> 00:10:12,304
No, just come to the park directly.

147
00:10:12,328 --> 00:10:17,828
Then I'll try going this Sunday.

148
00:10:17,851 --> 00:10:21,559
I'll be waiting!

149
00:10:21,582 --> 00:10:24,682
I appreciate your help.

150
00:10:24,705 --> 00:10:29,045
Let's do our best together!

151
00:10:29,068 --> 00:10:30,568
Scene 5: Planning a Day Trip for Work

152
00:10:30,568 --> 00:10:36,537
Tomorrow's business trip is to Osaka, right?

153
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:40,996
Yes, I'll take the Shinkansen there and back.

154
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:44,720
Are you staying overnight starting today?

155
00:10:44,743 --> 00:10:49,822
No, it's a day trip.

156
00:10:49,846 --> 00:10:55,279
A day trip? That must be tough.

157
00:10:55,302 --> 00:11:02,140
My wife is on a business trip, so I'll take care of the kids instead.

158
00:11:02,163 --> 00:11:08,339
I see. So your wife is also on a business trip?

159
00:11:08,363 --> 00:11:15,297
Yes. That's why I can't leave home.

160
00:11:15,321 --> 00:11:19,155
That makes sense.

161
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:25,545
I'll take the 6 AM Shinkansen tomorrow.

162
00:11:25,569 --> 00:11:29,936
You'll have to wake up early, huh?

163
00:11:29,959 --> 00:11:34,792
Yeah. The meeting starts at 10 AM.

164
00:11:34,815 --> 00:11:39,648
When do you think you'll be back?

165
00:11:39,671 --> 00:11:44,571
Probably around 5 PM.

166
00:11:44,594 --> 00:11:49,027
Are you taking the Shinkansen soon?

167
00:11:49,050 --> 00:11:55,150
Yes. I want to get home before the trains get too crowded.

168
00:11:55,173 --> 00:11:59,140
Trains are packed at night, after all.

169
00:11:59,164 --> 00:12:03,831
I should be home by around 8.

170
00:12:03,854 --> 00:12:07,888
Be careful on your way there and back.

171
00:12:07,911 --> 00:12:10,744
Thank you so much.

172
00:12:10,767 --> 00:12:16,041
I’m looking forward to your souvenir from Osaka!

173
00:12:16,064 --> 00:12:19,298
What would you like?

174
00:12:19,322 --> 00:12:24,074
Something like takoyaki-flavored snacks would be great.

175
00:12:24,097 --> 00:12:29,288
Got it. I’ll look for them at the station.

176
00:12:29,312 --> 00:12:34,688
Write it down before you forget!

177
00:12:34,711 --> 00:12:38,978
It’s fine. I’ll remember.

178
00:12:39,001 --> 00:12:43,547
Well then, do your best tomorrow!

179
00:12:43,571 --> 00:12:47,540
Okay. I’m off!

180
00:12:47,564 --> 00:12:51,043
You must be tired.

181
00:12:51,066 --> 00:12:54,013
Excuse me.

182
00:12:54,036 --> 00:12:55,536
Scene 6: Considering a Job Change

183
00:12:55,536 --> 00:13:02,469
You look serious while flipping through a job magazine.

184
00:13:02,492 --> 00:13:05,072
Yeah.

185
00:13:05,096 --> 00:13:10,277
I’m thinking about quitting my current part-time job.

186
00:13:10,301 --> 00:13:14,436
The part-time job at the izakaya, right?

187
00:13:14,459 --> 00:13:17,959
Why are you quitting?

188
00:13:17,982 --> 00:13:25,082
I’ve been working late a lot lately, and I’m feeling exhausted.

189
00:13:25,105 --> 00:13:28,291
I see.

190
00:13:28,314 --> 00:13:33,214
Yeah, you always look sleepy.

191
00:13:33,237 --> 00:13:35,871
Yeah.

192
00:13:35,894 --> 00:13:42,972
I don’t want to overwork myself and get sick, so I’d like to take a break.

193
00:13:42,995 --> 00:13:47,767
What kind of job are you looking for next?

194
00:13:47,791 --> 00:13:54,870
I’m torn between moving work or teaching English at a cram school.

195
00:13:54,894 --> 00:13:58,879
Those are totally different jobs.

196
00:13:58,902 --> 00:14:03,169
Does moving work pay well?

197
00:14:03,192 --> 00:14:05,776
Yeah.

198
00:14:05,799 --> 00:14:13,066
But I’ve heard it’s tough on the body and you might hurt your back.

199
00:14:13,089 --> 00:14:16,722
That sounds worrying.

200
00:14:16,745 --> 00:14:21,212
How about teaching English?

201
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:26,072
It’s a job teaching English to kids.

202
00:14:26,095 --> 00:14:33,328
It sounds fun, but preparing for lessons might leave you sleep-deprived.

203
00:14:33,351 --> 00:14:37,189
That’s true.

204
00:14:37,212 --> 00:14:43,846
But since I like kids, I think it could be enjoyable.

205
00:14:43,869 --> 00:14:49,744
In that case, you should go for a job you really like!

206
00:14:49,767 --> 00:14:52,200
Yeah.

207
00:14:52,223 --> 00:14:58,003
It’s better to choose a job that suits you rather than just the money.

208
00:14:58,027 --> 00:15:05,618
But if I teach English, I’ll need to study too.

209
00:15:05,641 --> 00:15:12,511
I’ve been slacking off on studying English lately, so this might be perfect.

210
00:15:12,534 --> 00:15:18,087
Then it’s settled—you’ll go for the English teaching job!

211
00:15:18,111 --> 00:15:23,483
I’ll call and apply for it tomorrow.

212
00:15:23,506 --> 00:15:28,540
I should also prepare thoroughly for the interview.

213
00:15:28,563 --> 00:15:35,108
I always get nervous before interviews, so I’m a little anxious now.

214
00:15:35,131 --> 00:15:42,118
Before the interview, it’s best to take deep breaths and relax.

215
00:15:42,142 --> 00:15:45,375
Yeah, that’s right.

216
00:15:45,398 --> 00:15:49,565
I’ll write my resume early too.

217
00:15:49,588 --> 00:15:57,299
It’s best to get your ID photo taken at a photo studio rather than a machine at the station.

218
00:15:57,323 --> 00:16:03,281
If you take it yourself, your expression tends to look gloomy.

219
00:16:03,305 --> 00:16:06,093
Exactly.

220
00:16:06,116 --> 00:16:10,450
First impressions are important, after all.

221
00:16:10,473 --> 00:16:17,173
It's been a while since I last wore a tie, so I'll practice beforehand.

222
00:16:17,196 --> 00:16:23,075
I don't usually wear one, so I tend to forget how to tie it.

223
00:16:23,098 --> 00:16:25,287
Yeah.

224
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:30,077
Thanks for all the advice!

225
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:34,857
Let me treat you to something once I get the job!

226
00:16:34,881 --> 00:16:37,547
Understood.

227
00:16:37,570 --> 00:16:41,604
I'll do my best at the interview.

228
00:16:41,626 --> 00:16:43,126
Scene 7: Homemade Bento for Better Health

229
00:16:43,126 --> 00:16:49,236
You’ve been bringing your own bento lately, huh?

230
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:51,493
Yeah.

231
00:16:51,516 --> 00:16:56,235
I’ve been making it myself since last month.

232
00:16:56,259 --> 00:16:59,359
Good for you!

233
00:16:59,381 --> 00:17:02,851
Do you wake up early?

234
00:17:02,875 --> 00:17:05,453
Yeah.

235
00:17:05,476 --> 00:17:09,748
I wake up at 6 every morning.

236
00:17:09,772 --> 00:17:13,438
Isn’t cooking difficult?

237
00:17:13,461 --> 00:17:19,495
The more you cook, the more fun it gets.

238
00:17:19,517 --> 00:17:22,831
I see.

239
00:17:22,855 --> 00:17:29,955
I think my body felt sluggish because I was eating out too much lately.

240
00:17:29,978 --> 00:17:33,978
So you switched to bringing your own bento?

241
00:17:34,001 --> 00:17:36,901
Yeah.

242
00:17:36,924 --> 00:17:41,024
I started doing it for my health.

243
00:17:41,047 --> 00:17:44,355
How’s your body feeling now?

244
00:17:44,379 --> 00:17:51,926
As I get used to the bento routine, my body feels lighter.

245
00:17:51,949 --> 00:17:55,506
That’s great to hear!

246
00:17:55,530 --> 00:17:59,907
And it saves money too.

247
00:17:59,930 --> 00:18:04,964
How much do you save per month?

248
00:18:04,987 --> 00:18:08,920
About 10,000 yen, I think.

249
00:18:08,943 --> 00:18:12,896
That’s a lot!

250
00:18:12,919 --> 00:18:19,386
The more I save, the more my savings grow—I’m happy about that.

251
00:18:19,409 --> 00:18:24,042
Maybe I’ll start making my own bento too.

252
00:18:24,065 --> 00:18:28,704
You absolutely should!

253
00:18:28,727 --> 00:18:33,699
But I’m not good at waking up early.

254
00:18:33,723 --> 00:18:38,556
It’s easier if you prepare things the night before.

255
00:18:38,579 --> 00:18:42,346
What kind of things do you prepare?

256
00:18:42,369 --> 00:18:48,108
I cook rice and chop vegetables ahead of time.

257
00:18:48,132 --> 00:18:50,965
I see.

258
00:18:50,988 --> 00:18:54,337
That sounds doable.

259
00:18:54,361 --> 00:19:00,138
You could also make side dishes on the weekend and freeze them.

260
00:19:00,161 --> 00:19:04,028
I’ll give it a try starting tomorrow.

261
00:19:04,051 --> 00:19:07,284
Good luck!

262
00:19:07,307 --> 00:19:11,774
If you have any questions, just ask.

263
00:19:11,797 --> 00:19:14,939
Of course!

264
00:19:14,962 --> 00:19:16,462
Scene 8: Planning the Sports Tournament Prizes

265
00:19:16,462 --> 00:19:22,329
Let’s decide on the prizes for the upcoming sports tournament.

266
00:19:22,352 --> 00:19:26,295
The prizes for the winning team, right?

267
00:19:26,319 --> 00:19:31,152
Yes, what do you think would be good?

268
00:19:31,175 --> 00:19:35,966
Last year, it was towels and tea.

269
00:19:35,989 --> 00:19:41,135
Do you think we should do the same this year?

270
00:19:41,158 --> 00:19:49,258
Towels are fine, but compared to tea, people would be happier with a coffee set.

271
00:19:49,281 --> 00:19:54,874
You’re right, let’s go with a coffee set.

272
00:19:54,898 --> 00:20:00,769
Shouldn’t we also include a bookstore gift card as the top prize?

273
00:20:00,793 --> 00:20:04,188
A bookstore gift card?

274
00:20:04,211 --> 00:20:10,344
Yes, you can buy not just books but magazines too.

275
00:20:10,367 --> 00:20:13,667
That’s a great idea!

276
00:20:13,690 --> 00:20:17,684
Which gift card would you like?

277
00:20:17,708 --> 00:20:21,941
How about 1,000 yen?

278
00:20:21,964 --> 00:20:25,912
That fits within the budget.

279
00:20:25,936 --> 00:20:29,636
What about the participation prizes?

280
00:20:29,659 --> 00:20:34,779
Let’s give out snacks as prizes.

281
00:20:34,802 --> 00:20:38,541
I think chocolate would be great.

282
00:20:38,565 --> 00:20:45,131
Unlike summer, chocolate won’t melt in winter, right?

283
00:20:45,154 --> 00:20:49,592
Yeah, let’s grab some at the supermarket.

284
00:20:49,616 --> 00:20:53,559
When are we going shopping?

285
00:20:53,583 --> 00:20:57,616
Let’s go tomorrow evening.

286
00:20:57,639 --> 00:21:02,539
Got it, I’ll get the car ready.

287
00:21:02,562 --> 00:21:07,068
Thanks, that’ll really help.

288
00:21:07,092 --> 00:21:11,200
We’ll have a lot to carry, huh?

289
00:21:11,224 --> 00:21:15,617
Should we wrap the prizes nicely?

290
00:21:15,640 --> 00:21:20,186
Yes, let’s add some ribbons.

291
00:21:20,210 --> 00:21:23,877
Preparations are going to be tough, aren’t they?

292
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:28,766
I hope everyone will be happy with them.

293
00:21:28,789 --> 00:21:32,896
Yeah, let’s do our best!

294
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:38,994
Alright, let’s meet at the parking lot at 5 tomorrow.

295
00:21:39,017 --> 00:21:42,383
Understood.

296
00:21:42,406 --> 00:21:43,906
Scene 9: Strange Odor from a Heater / Handling Heater Issues

297
00:21:43,906 --> 00:21:49,878
This heater is giving off a weird smell.

298
00:21:49,902 --> 00:21:52,469
Yeah, it really is.

299
00:21:52,492 --> 00:21:56,525
It smells like something’s burning.

300
00:21:56,548 --> 00:22:00,657
It might be broken.

301
00:22:00,681 --> 00:22:05,551
It’s dangerous—you should turn it off right away.

302
00:22:05,574 --> 00:22:10,173
But if we turn it off, it’ll get cold.

303
00:22:10,197 --> 00:22:16,307
That’s exactly why we need to use it safely.

304
00:22:16,330 --> 00:22:21,129
What happens if we keep using it?

305
00:22:21,152 --> 00:22:25,419
There’s a risk of a fire.

306
00:22:25,442 --> 00:22:28,675
That’s scary.

307
00:22:28,698 --> 00:22:31,768
I’ll turn it off right now.

308
00:22:31,792 --> 00:22:35,225
Should we get it repaired?

309
00:22:35,248 --> 00:22:40,686
Wouldn’t it be cheaper to just buy a new one?

310
00:22:40,710 --> 00:22:46,257
We won’t know until we have it checked by an electrician.

311
00:22:46,281 --> 00:22:50,316
Where’s the warranty?

312
00:22:50,339 --> 00:22:54,872
It should be in the drawer.

313
00:22:54,895 --> 00:22:57,762
Found it!

314
00:22:57,785 --> 00:23:01,652
You bought this last winter, huh?

315
00:23:01,675 --> 00:23:07,441
So it might still be covered under warranty.

316
00:23:07,464 --> 00:23:11,257
Should I call and ask?

317
00:23:11,281 --> 00:23:13,674
Yeah.

318
00:23:13,697 --> 00:23:17,330
I’ll make the call.

319
00:23:17,353 --> 00:23:20,857
Okay, thanks!

320
00:23:20,881 --> 00:23:27,181
Hello, I’d like to request a repair for my heater.

321
00:23:27,204 --> 00:23:29,996
Yes, what's up?

322
00:23:30,019 --> 00:23:32,786
Yes, what's up?

323
00:23:32,810 --> 00:23:35,848
What are they saying?

324
00:23:35,871 --> 00:23:40,538
They said they’ll come by tomorrow afternoon.

325
00:23:40,561 --> 00:23:45,137
So we can’t use the heater until then.

326
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:49,279
We’ll have to rely on the air conditioner.

327
00:23:49,302 --> 00:23:53,602
Did you clean the air conditioner’s filter?

328
00:23:53,625 --> 00:23:58,392
I cleaned it last week, so it should be fine.

329
00:23:58,415 --> 00:24:02,525
Let's turn on the air conditioner.

330
00:24:02,549 --> 00:24:06,501
Hope the repair cost isn't too high.

331
00:24:06,525 --> 00:24:09,592
Yeah, I hope so.

332
00:24:09,615 --> 00:24:14,330
Let's tough it out until tomorrow.

333
00:24:24,362 --> 00:24:25,862
Scene 10: Reflections on the Speech Contest

334
00:24:25,862 --> 00:24:31,162
Congrats on finishing the speech contest!

335
00:24:31,185 --> 00:24:34,151
Thank you so much.

336
00:24:34,174 --> 00:24:37,754
I was so nervous.

337
00:24:37,778 --> 00:24:42,920
You did an amazing job—so confident and impressive!

338
00:24:42,944 --> 00:24:48,977
Thanks to your guidance, I managed to finish my speech.

339
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:53,712
What was the hardest part for you?

340
00:24:53,736 --> 00:25:00,074
It was tough keeping eye contact with everyone.

341
00:25:00,097 --> 00:25:04,564
You were looking up a lot, though!

342
00:25:04,587 --> 00:25:09,823
I blanked out halfway and panicked.

343
00:25:09,847 --> 00:25:14,514
But you stayed calm and started over.

344
00:25:14,537 --> 00:25:21,652
I thought, 'Even if I fail, I won’t give up halfway.'

345
00:25:21,675 --> 00:25:25,942
That’s the right mindset.

346
00:25:25,965 --> 00:25:31,465
My friends told me I should join again next year.

347
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:35,472
You absolutely should!

348
00:25:35,496 --> 00:25:41,806
Next time, I want to try a longer speech.

349
00:25:41,829 --> 00:25:46,200
Your pronunciation has really improved!

350
00:25:46,223 --> 00:25:51,356
It’s all thanks to practicing out loud every day.

351
00:25:51,379 --> 00:25:56,556
That effort will definitely pay off.

352
00:25:56,580 --> 00:26:01,813
I want to get even better at Japanese.

353
00:26:01,836 --> 00:26:07,536
Do you have any new goals?

354
00:26:07,559 --> 00:26:14,316
My parents want me to be able to understand Japanese news.

355
00:26:14,340 --> 00:26:17,674
That’s a great goal!

356
00:26:17,697 --> 00:26:22,174
I’ll make sure to watch TV every day.

357
00:26:22,197 --> 00:26:27,141
If there’s a word you don’t know, just ask me.

358
00:26:27,165 --> 00:26:31,521
Okay! Thanks so much.

359
00:26:31,545 --> 00:26:36,245
Take it easy and rest up today.

360
00:26:36,268 --> 00:26:39,305
Thank you so much.

361
00:26:39,328 --> 00:26:44,767
Make sure to share this with the class too!

362
00:26:44,791 --> 00:26:49,691
I’ll tell everyone in tomorrow’s lesson.

363
00:26:49,714 --> 00:26:53,022
Looking forward to it!

364
00:26:53,045 --> 00:26:57,145
Alright, I’ll take my leave now.